    "q-70649": {
      "dom_id": "step-q70649",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "What are the radius $r$ and the coordinates of the center $C$ for the sphere ${x}^{2}+(y+5)^{2}+{z}^{2}=10?$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the equation of a sphere centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ with radius $r>0$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-{x}_{0})^{2}+(y-{y}_{0})^{2}+(z-{z}_{0})^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe can write our equation as\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+(y-(-5))^{2}+{z}^{2}=(\\sqrt{10})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich gives us the center at the point point $C(0,-5,0)$ and the radius $r=\\sqrt{10}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
