    "q-164263": {
      "dom_id": "step-q164263",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Given the ellipsoid $\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{1}+\\frac{(z+2)^{2}}{8}=1$, find its intercepts with the $y$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the $y$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{1}+\\frac{(0+2)^{2}}{8} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{1}+\\frac{4}{8} & =1 \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ y-2 & =\\pm \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ y & =2\\pm \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $y=\\frac{3}{2}$ and $y=\\frac{5}{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $y$-axis are $(0,\\frac{3}{2},0)$ and $(0,\\frac{5}{2},0).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
