    "q-70488": {
      "dom_id": "step-q70488",
      "name": "Question 17",
      "problem": "What is the projection of the intersection between the sphere $(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=9$ and the plane $z=1$ onto the $xy$-plane.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the intersection of the sphere and the plane $z=1$, we substitute $z=1$ into the equation of the sphere:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+(1)^{2} & =9 \\\\ (x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+1 & =9 \\\\ (x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =8 \\\\ (x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nProjecting this onto the $xy$-plane gives us the equation of the circle of radius $2\\sqrt{2}$ centered at $(-2,0).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
